  "body": "Comment by Claude:\n\n> [Preload](https://html.spec.whatwg.org/multipage/links.html#preload) says:\n>\n>> If *options*'s destination is \"`image`\" and *options*'s source set is not null, then set *options*'s href to the result of selecting an image source from *options*'s source set.\n>\n> But [select an image source from a source set](https://html.spec.whatwg.org/multipage/images.html#select-an-image-source-from-a-source-set) returns an image source and its pixel density, not a URL string, so *options*'s href ends up as a tuple.\n>\n> Maybe it should set *options*'s href to the selected image source's URL and ignore the pixel density. (Found while working on #13046, which adds a source size to the return value.)\n",
